Usage: fva run <file.wasm> [options] [-- <arguments>...]

Run a WASI command on FVA's verified machine and its verified WASI host. The program
gets the arguments after --, with the file name of the module as argument 0. FVA reads
standard input and every --dir directory before the program starts, and writes the
changed files back when the program stops. The clocks read 0. FVA supports the 20 WASI
calls of its model. The module must export _start (no parameters, no results) and its
memory, and must have no start function and no _initialize export.

Options:
  --dir HOST[::GUEST]   Give the program the directory HOST, under the name GUEST
                        (default: HOST as written). You can give this option more
                        than once. The directories must not overlap. FVA accepts
                        regular files and directories only.
  --env NAME=VALUE      Add an environment variable. You can give this option more
                        than once; FVA keeps the order and duplicate names.
  --random HEX          Give these bytes to every random_get call (cut or padded with
                        zeros), in place of fresh random bytes.
  --fuel N              Stop after N machine steps.

Exit status: the program's exit status (statuses from 126 on are reported as 1), 0
when _start returns, 134 when the program traps, 1 for an exception that no handler
catches, 2 when FVA cannot run or finish the program (the message names the cause).
